    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "The Moab Fault is a salt structure-related, well developed normal fault in east-central Utah displaying a complex geometry. Preliminary field investigation discovered four apparent deformation mechanisms operating along the Moab fault. The objective of this study is to delineate the spatial and temporal relationships between these mechanisms along the length of the fault, in order to understand the development and internal architecture of the fault Detailed field study, petrographic work and computer modeling will be undertaken to meet this objective. The results of this study can then be employed to evaluate other faults with similar characteristics, including those located in the subsurface.",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        },
